{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":54724,"items":[{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00762","title":["Towards Universal and Lightweight Coverless Image Steganography with Multimodal Large Language Models Assistance"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00762","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:28:46Z","timestamp":1791487726000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698335.pdf?arnumber=11698335","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"abstract":"<jats:p>The huge amount of parameters, high memory occupation, long reasoning delay and difficult adaptation of hardware environment have become important factors that restrict large models from entering the engineering site and edge equipment. In order to solve the above problems, this article proposes a large model lightweight compression and reasoning performance optimization method for engineering deployment. Based on the importance of parameters, this method integrates pruning, quantification and distillation compression models. Simultaneously optimize the reasoning strategies such as KV Cache management and operator fusion to improve the response speed and throughput under limited hardware. The experiment builds a test environment based on the 7B parameter-level universal language model, and compares it from the aspects of model size, memory occupation, first Token delay, generation throughput and task accuracy. The results show that the proposed method reduces the model file size to 32.4% of the original model, reduces the peak memory occupation by 51.7%, and increases the average generation throughput by about 1.91 times when the accuracy of engineering question answering task is only reduced by 1.6 percentage points. Joint compression and reasoning optimization can achieve a good balance between performance maintenance and resource saving, which can provide reference for the application of large-scale model in industrial field, privatization deployment and edge intelligent system.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1117\/12.3135043","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,19]],"date-time":"2026-10-19T18:12:06Z","timestamp":1792433526000},"title":["Lightweight compression and inference performance optimization methods for large models aimed at engineering deployment"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2209-0601","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Rong","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Baolan","family":"Liang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Qi","family":"Wen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.spiedigitallibrary.org\/conference-proceedings-of-spie\/14516\/3135043\/Lightweight-compression-and-inference-performance-optimization-methods-for-large-models\/10.1117\/12.3135043.full","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1117\/12.3135043","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,19]]}},{"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>We present TDepth, a lightweight hybrid model for monocular depth estimation trained using teacher\u2010generated pseudo labels. TDepth combines a small CNN backbone, a local\u2010global transformer encoder, an attention\u2010guided skip\u2010fusion decoder, a bin\u2010based depth head and a lightweight refiner for improving boundaries and thin structures. To avoid dependence on expensive sensor depth during training, we generate pseudo depth labels offline using Pixel\u2010Perfect\u2010Depth and train on about 550K images from NYU Depth v2 and ScanNet++. We evaluate TDepth on in\u2010domain, zero\u2010shot and efficiency settings. On NYU Depth v2, TDepth\u2010Full achieves , AbsRel  and RMSE , while the smaller 15.1M\u2010parameter variant remains competitive with much lower model complexity. In zero\u2010shot evaluation, TDepth\u2010Full achieves  and AbsRel  on iBims\u20101 and  and AbsRel  on SUN\u2010RGBD, showing strong transfer to unseen indoor datasets. TDepth\u2010Small reaches about 240\u00a0FPS at  and remains above 30\u00a0FPS even at , while TDepth\u2010Full reaches 60\u00a0FPS at  and provides stronger depth accuracy with a practical runtime profile. These results show that TDepth provides a strong balance between depth accuracy, zero\u2010shot generalisation and computational efficiency, making it a practical option for lightweight monocular depth estimation.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1049\/cvi2.70088","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,13]],"date-time":"2026-10-13T06:18:36Z","timestamp":1791872316000},"title":["TDepth: A Lightweight Hybrid Model for Monocular Depth Estimation"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3593-7448","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Muhammad Adeel","family":"Hafeez","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Visual Intelligence Lab &amp; Machine Learning Group School of Computer Science and Data Science Institute University of Galway  Galway Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ganesh","family":"Sistu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Valeo Vision Systems  Tuam Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Michael G.","family":"Madden","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Machine Learning Group &amp; Visual Intelligence Lab School of Computer Science University of Galway  Galway Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7964-5199","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ihsan","family":"Ullah","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Visual Intelligence Lab &amp; Machine Learning Group School of Computer Science and Data Science Institute University of Galway  Galway Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1049\/cvi2.70088","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/full-xml\/10.1049\/cvi2.70088","content-type":"application\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1049\/cvi2.70088","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1049\/cvi2.70088","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,1]]}},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.cviu.2026.104976","title":["Efficient semantic segmentation via Lightweight Multiple-Information Interaction Network"],"author":[{"given":"Yangyang","family":"Qiu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Guoan","family":"Xu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Guangwei","family":"Gao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Baihua","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yi","family":"Yu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.cviu.2026.104976","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,11]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T20:43:43Z","timestamp":1791319423000},"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S1077314226003437?httpAccept=text\/xml","content-type":"text\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S1077314226003437?httpAccept=text\/plain","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icnpcv69434.2026.11708984","title":["Lightweight Models for Emotion Recognition in Edge Ai Applications"],"author":[{"given":"B","family":"C.Divakara","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Global Academy of Technology","place":["Bengaluru, Karnataka, India"],"department":["Department of ECE"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Bhanu Prakash","family":"Pandiri","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Central Missouri","place":["West Allis, Wisconsin, USA"],"department":["Department of Information Technology"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sandeep","family":"Belidhe","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"San Francisco Bay University","place":["Duluth, Georgia, USA"],"department":["Department of Information Technology"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Santosh","family":"Jaini","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The University of Texas at Tyler","place":["Garner, North Carolina, USA"],"department":["Department of Information Technology"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Vijaya Vardan Reddy S","family":"P","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"R.M.K. Engineering College","place":["Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India"],"department":["Department of EC-ACT"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Madhava Rao","family":"Karri","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Centurion university of Technology and Management","place":["Vizianagaram, Andhra Pradesh, India"],"department":["Department of ECE"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icnpcv69434.2026.11708984","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,7]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]],"date-time":"2026-10-07T19:24:36Z","timestamp":1791401076000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11707819\/11708741\/11708984.pdf?arnumber=11708984","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-032-37447-9_22","title":["Lightweight Online Reinforcement Learning for\u00a0Block Decomposition of\u00a0CAD Models"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-7818-356X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xitong","family":"Luo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0006-6408-5308","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Zhenghan","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0009-1684-9491","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yucong","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1767-789X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yi","family":"Cai","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-3-032-37447-9_22","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,8]],"date-time":"2026-09-08T15:52:11Z","timestamp":1788882731000},"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/978-3-032-37447-9_22","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/iccvdm71812.2026.11709374","title":["AVLF-Nav: Embodied Object Navigation via Active Visual Exploration and Lightweight Vision\u2013Language Fusion"],"author":[{"given":"Nachuan","family":"Wang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Southwest Jiaotong University","place":["Chengdu, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/iccvdm71812.2026.11709374","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,8]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,1]],"date-time":"2026-10-01T19:10:27Z","timestamp":1790881827000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11709023\/11709058\/11709374.pdf?arnumber=11709374","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00579","title":["TextBind: Your Vision-Language Models are Naturally Unified Multimodal Models"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00579","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:19:51Z","timestamp":1791487191000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11697947.pdf?arnumber=11697947","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Background<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>Visual foundation models (VFMs) and vision-language models (VLMs) offer adaptable approaches to neurosurgical imaging, segmentation, intraoperative assistance, and clinical decision support. However, the available evidence varies substantially in model type, supervision, validation setting, and clinical task, and their readiness for routine clinical use remains uncertain.<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Methods<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>We conducted a narrative review of peer-reviewed primary research reports published between January 2020 and August 2026, identified through PubMed, IEEE Xplore, and Google Scholar. Studies evaluating visual, vision-language, or multimodal foundation models in neurosurgical applications were included. Supervised Vision Transformer (ViT) and ViT\u2013CNN systems were retained as contemporary transformer-based comparator studies but were not classified as foundation models. Evidence was synthesised according to model adaptation, clinical application, within-study comparative performance, validation setting, and translational limitations.<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Results<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>Seven studies met the review criteria. FastGlioma provided a prospective multicentre evaluation of a visual foundation model for intraoperative detection of glioma infiltration. In lumbar-spine MRI, zero-shot SAM and MedSAM performed below supervised nnU-Net on segmentation metrics. A task-adapted SAM2-UNet system achieved a mean Dice score of 0.771 for brain-tumour segmentation, although its mean IoU was 0.569 compared with 0.571 for Mask R-CNN in the reported comparison. Supervised transformer-based systems demonstrated performance in acute traumatic brain injury triage and vertebral fracture classification, although the latter combined ViT, CNN, ensemble fusion, and GAN-based augmentation. In multimodal reasoning, GPT-4o achieved higher absolute diagnostic accuracy than CNS-Obsidian, whereas CNS-Obsidian had higher length-adjusted diagnostic accuracy. Evidence for clinical translation remained limited by heterogeneous validation settings, incomplete reporting of computational performance and safety outcomes, predominantly single-centre or preclinical evaluations, and limited assessment of patient outcomes.<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Conclusion<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>Foundation-model-based systems show potential across selected neurosurgical tasks, but current evidence is insufficient to establish routine clinical readiness or patient benefit. Reported results are primarily task-specific and should not be interpreted as evidence of a general architectural advantage. Future studies should evaluate these systems prospectively under human supervision while determining whether clinicians can reliably detect and mitigate erroneous outputs. Multi-centre validation, uncertainty assessment, computational efficiency, workflow integration, and patient-centred outcomes should be prioritised.<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>","DOI":"10.1007\/s44584-026-00008-7","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]],"date-time":"2026-10-21T13:13:43Z","timestamp":1792588423000},"title":["Vision-language models and visual foundation models in neurosurgery"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0000-3429-6522","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Godswill","family":"Uzoechina","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0008-9631-1845","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Treasure","family":"Osajiuba","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Elochukwu","family":"Marvellous","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/s44584-026-00008-7.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/link.springer.com\/article\/10.1007\/s44584-026-00008-7","content-type":"text\/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/s44584-026-00008-7.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s44584-026-00008-7","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]]}},{"abstract":"<jats:p>To overcome the trade-off between constrained on-board computation of edge devices like AGVs in smart warehousing and logistics and the high real-time demands of visual perception, this paper proposes a lightweight object-detection system based on the Jetson Nano. The ultra-lightweight YOLOv5n network is chosen as the detector; a special dataset is gathered to train the model on unstructured industrial-logistics scenes; and Mosaic data augmentation is applied during training to enhance performance in challenging environments. To reduce the impact of the compute and memory-bandwidth limitations of the target platform, we propose a co-optimization approach that uses lower-resolution input, TensorRT operator fusion, and FP16 half-precision quantization. Our experiments demonstrate that the proposed system is significantly more robust to lighting variations and multiple targets than a traditional OpenCV pipeline. On the Jetson Nano, the fine-tuned model achieves mAP@0.5 = 99.5 % on the test set, with single-frame inference-only latency decreased from 44.42 ms to 23.17 ms and inference-only throughput of 43.83 FPS. The model has 1.9 M parameters, which provides a good trade-off between compute, power, and real-time performance on the edge device, and a consistent deployment pattern for the visual subsystems of industrial mobile robots.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1117\/12.3126215","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T16:57:34Z","timestamp":1791305854000},"title":["Design and implementation of a lightweight vision system for edge-computing AGVs"],"author":[{"given":"Ping","family":"Jiang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.spiedigitallibrary.org\/conference-proceedings-of-spie\/14353\/3126215\/Design-and-implementation-of-a-lightweight-vision-system-for-edge\/10.1117\/12.3126215.full","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1117\/12.3126215","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]]}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00676","title":["Object-Centric Vision Token Pruning for Vision Language Models"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00676","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:17:07Z","timestamp":1791487027000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698146.pdf?arnumber=11698146","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00925","title":["Mitigating Vision-Text Order Bias in Vision-Language Models"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00925","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:18:09Z","timestamp":1791487089000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698501.pdf?arnumber=11698501","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7528332","title":["ISSC-ReID: Asymmetric collaboration between lightweight and vision-language models for cattle body-surface re-identification"],"author":[{"given":"Zejun","family":"Wen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6059-7035","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"YongSheng","family":"Qi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jiaying","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Liqiang","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Tongmei","family":"Jing","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"abstract":"<jats:p>Cattle body-surface re-identification is challenged by pose variation, occlusion, and spatially dispersed identity cues in animals with similar coat colors. We propose ISSC-ReID, an asymmetric collaboration framework combining a lightweight identity-discriminative model with frozen Contrastive Language\u2013Image Pre-training (CLIP) encoders. EdgeFace-ISEM provides identity-supervised visual features, while CLIP supplies global image features and attribute responses. The two visual similarities jointly determine a fixed Top-K candidate set; attribute semantics are restricted to calibrating candidates within this set. An identity structure enhancement module (ISEM) combines parallel structural and texture-response branches through channel-wise adaptive fusion and a residual connection. At the decision level, weak semantic evidence is incorporated through asymmetric reliability discounting, visual-prioritized conflict redistribution, ignorance mass retention, and uncertainty-gated iterative calibration. On a self-collected dataset containing 7,091 identities and 191,457 images, ISSC-ReID achieves a mean average precision of 94.42% and Rank-1, Rank-5, and Rank-10 accuracies of 92.62%, 97.58%, and 98.75%, respectively, under an identity-disjoint, identity-prototype retrieval protocol. These results exceed the strongest corresponding baseline among six comparison methods by 3.90, 4.42, 3.68, and 3.15 percentage points. The ablation results support the contribution of ISEM and the combined evidence-calibration module to cattle identity retrieval.<\/jats:p>","URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7528332","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,26]],"date-time":"2026-09-26T13:44:09Z","timestamp":1790430249000}},{"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Multi\u2010modal reasoning enhanced by large language models is central to developing vision\u2010language models (VLMs). However, existing methods ignore extracting local details with global context when handling complex vision\u2010language tasks. This study introduces a novel In\u2010Context Learning into Chain\u2010of\u2010Thought reasoning (IC2T) framework, adopting a staged reasoning mechanism that progressively optimises the integration of local and global features to satisfy the demands of complex tasks. The IC2T dynamically extracts the regions of interest as the local information and the entire vision as the global information, which are then fused and stepped into multi\u2010round reasoning. The proposed in\u2010context learning scheme retrieves similar samples and uses their global and local information to provide contextual guidance for progressive reasoning. The extensive experimental results demonstrate that IC2T based on multi\u2010scale VLMs outperforms state\u2010of\u2010the\u2010art models across multiple multi\u2010modal benchmarks, and extensive ablation studies highlight the critical roles of the proposed in\u2010context learning and chain\u2010of\u2010thought reasoning in improving logical reasoning performance.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1049\/cvi2.70087","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,11]],"date-time":"2026-10-11T18:45:41Z","timestamp":1791744341000},"title":["IC2T: Embedding In\u2010Context Learning Into Chain of Thought for Vision\u2010Language Models"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-1973-4573","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jing","family":"Liang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology Huazhong University of Science and Technology  Wuhan Hubei China"},{"name":"Hubei University of Education  Wuhan Hubei China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Rui","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology Huazhong University of Science and Technology  Wuhan Hubei China"},{"name":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Manufacturing Equipment Digitization Guangdong HUST Industrial Technology Research Institute  Dongguan China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yixue","family":"Hao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology Huazhong University of Science and Technology  Wuhan Hubei China"},{"name":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Manufacturing Equipment Digitization Guangdong HUST Industrial Technology Research Institute  Dongguan China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Tao","family":"Guan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology Huazhong University of Science and Technology  Wuhan Hubei China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1049\/cvi2.70087","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/full-xml\/10.1049\/cvi2.70087","content-type":"application\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/ietresearch.onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1049\/cvi2.70087","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1049\/cvi2.70087","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,1]]}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00174","title":["Vision Language Models are Confused Tourists"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00174","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:16:46Z","timestamp":1791487006000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698205.pdf?arnumber=11698205","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00534","title":["When Models Learn to Ask Why: Adaptive Causal Reasoning for Trustworthy Medical Vision-Language Models"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00534","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:17:19Z","timestamp":1791487039000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11697696.pdf?arnumber=11697696","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00558","title":["Vision-R1: Evolving Human-Free Alignment in Large Vision-Language Models via Vision-Guided Reinforcement Learning"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00558","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:38:40Z","timestamp":1791488320000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698298.pdf?arnumber=11698298","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.23919\/aaicvcps00050.2026.00115","title":["ForestFire Detector: a Lightweight Detection Model for Forest fire Monitoring"],"author":[{"given":"Jun","family":"Yan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.23919\/aaicvcps00050.2026.00115","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,3]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,5]],"date-time":"2026-10-05T19:13:54Z","timestamp":1791227634000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11719634\/11719635\/11719784.pdf?arnumber=11719784","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/iccvdm71812.2026.11709345","title":["A Lightweight Improved YOLO11 for Small-Object Detection in UAV Imagery"],"author":[{"given":"Shihua","family":"Hou","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics","place":["Nanjing, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/iccvdm71812.2026.11709345","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,8]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,1]],"date-time":"2026-10-01T19:08:05Z","timestamp":1790881685000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11709023\/11709058\/11709345.pdf?arnumber=11709345","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00337","title":["BitTP: The Lightweight Trajectory Prediction Model with BitLLM for Edge-Devices"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00337","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:21:08Z","timestamp":1791487268000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698345.pdf?arnumber=11698345","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00284","title":["ProGIC: Progressive and Lightweight Generative Image Compression with Residual Vector Quantization"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00284","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:18:49Z","timestamp":1791487129000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11698221.pdf?arnumber=11698221","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}]},{"abstract":"<jats:p>Real-time object perception with geometric awareness is a critical enabling technology for intelligent visual perception in robotics. However, deploying robust visual recognition on resource-constrained edge devices remains challenging due to computational limitations and the lack of geometric priors. This paper presents a lightweight technology framework that integrates an improved AlexNet-based dual-branch network (SANet) with dilated convolutions and a geometry-informed loss function, enabling simultaneous object classification and geometric property inference from a single forward propagation. Unlike conventional end-to-end grasping methods, the proposed framework emphasizes system-level technology integration: it fuses RGB appearance with noise-free STL geometric priors during training, then discards the auxiliary branch at inference to maintain a low computational footprint suitable for embedded platforms. Experimental validation on a humanoid robot for automated manipulation tasks demonstrates high recognition accuracy (93\u201397%) and stable operation across varying object appearances, with an end-to-end processing time under 0.31 s on a consumer-grade GPU. The work provides an efficient, interpretable, and geometry-aware solution that advances intelligent perception technologies in robotics and automation.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1117\/12.3127215","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]],"date-time":"2026-10-06T16:57:17Z","timestamp":1791305837000},"title":["SANet: lightweight geometry fusion for adaptive robotic grasping"],"author":[{"given":"Zongwen","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.spiedigitallibrary.org\/conference-proceedings-of-spie\/14353\/3127215\/SANet-lightweight-geometry-fusion-for-adaptive-robotic-grasping\/10.1117\/12.3127215.full","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1117\/12.3127215","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,6]]}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00071","title":["Phantasia: Context-Adaptive Backdoors in Vision Language Models"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/cvprf71909.2026.00071","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T19:29:10Z","timestamp":1791487750000},"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11697600\/11697601\/11697937.pdf?arnumbe